2026-10-17|Check Whether One String Can Be Transformed into Another

Question
Given strings s1 and s2 of equal length, return true if s1 can be transformed into s2 using the allowed movements. Otherwise, return false.

Approach

1. First, remove all '#' characters from both strings. If the resulting strings differ, the transformation is impossible because characters cannot cross each other or disappear.

2. Use two pointers to traverse s1 and s2, skipping all '#' characters.

3. Compare the positions of corresponding non-empty characters.

4. If the character is 'A', it can only move left. Therefore, its position in s2 must be less than or equal to its position in s1.

5. If the character is 'B', it can only move right. Therefore, its position in s2 must be greater than or equal to its position in s1.

6. If any character violates its movement restriction, return false.

7. If all corresponding characters satisfy these conditions, return true.

8. Time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the strings, because each character is processed at most once.

9. Space complexity is O(1) auxiliary space when using two pointers without creating additional strings.

Solution
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

class Solution {
public:
    bool canChange(string s1, string s2) {
        int n = s1.size();

        if (s2.size() != n) {
            return false;
        }

        int i = 0, j = 0;

        while (i < n && j < n) {
            while (i < n && s1[i] == '#') {
                i++;
            }

            while (j < n && s2[j] == '#') {
                j++;
            }

            if (i == n || j == n) {
                break;
            }

            if (s1[i] != s2[j]) {
                return false;
            }

            if (s1[i] == 'A' && i < j) {
                return false;
            }

            if (s1[i] == 'B' && i > j) {
                return false;
            }

            i++;
            j++;
        }

        while (i < n && s1[i] == '#') {
            i++;
        }

        while (j < n && s2[j] == '#') {
            j++;
        }

        return i == n && j == n;
    }
};

int main() {
    string s1, s2;
    cin >> s1 >> s2;

    Solution solution;

    cout << (solution.canChange(s1, s2) ? "true" : "false") << '\n';

    return 0;
}
```

Example

Input:
```text
#A#B##
A###B#
```

Output:
```text
true
```

Explanation:

- 'A' moves one position to the left.
- 'B' moves one position to the right.
- Neither character crosses the other.

Therefore, the transformation is possible.
